2026-10-19T22:24:24.6005216Z   ISSUE_NUMBER: 57216
2026-10-19T22:24:24.6005648Z   ISSUE_TITLE: [FEATURE]: Plugin API: read the session context size estimate
2026-10-19T22:24:24.6009428Z   ISSUE_BODY: ## Problem

The host calculates the session context size estimate. The estimate is private to the core. A plugin cannot read it.

## Source (v2.0.31)

- `packages/core/src/session/compaction.ts:874` gives the estimate:

  `export const estimateContext = (context: SessionContext.Loaded) => {`
- `packages/client/src/effect/api/api.ts:361` shows that the plugin context operation gives messages only:

  `export type SessionContextOutput = ReadonlyArray<SessionMessage.Info>`

  The output has no token estimate.

## Purpose

A plugin shows the context usage in a status line. A plugin selects compaction before the context overflows. The plugin must have the same estimate that the host uses.

## Proposed minimal API

Add the estimate to the plugin session domain, for example `ctx.session.contextSize({ sessionID })`. Give the measured and estimated token counts.

## What the plugin does today without it

The plugin cannot read the estimate. The plugin must approximate the size from the message text, and the approximation disagrees with the host.

